        ": \"يُقْتَلُ اَلْعَبْدُ بِالْحُرِّ وَ لاَ يُقْتَلُ اَلْحُرُّ بِالْعَبْدِ وَ لَكِنْ يُغَرَّمُ قِيمَتَهُ وَ يُضْرَبُ ضَرْباً شَدِيداً حَتَّى لاَ يَعُودَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5260 - Uthman ibn Isa narrated from Sama'ah that Abu Abdullah (as) said:\n\"A slave is to be killed for killing a free man, but a free man is not to be killed for killing a slave. However, he must pay the slave's value and be severely beaten so that he does not repeat such an act.\""
        ]
      }
